WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:15.051
Polly was sitting alone in the dining room when Nancy brought in supper.

2
00:00:15.071 --> 00:00:21.513
"My niece will have to suffer the consequences for being late," Aunt Polly said.

3
00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:26.555
"When Pollyanna comes downstairs, she may have bread and milk in the kitchen."

4
00:00:26.575 --> 00:00:28.735
"Yes, ma'am."

5
00:00:29.716 --> 00:00:33.374
Nancy made a face, but fortunately Aunt Polly didn't catch her.

6
00:00:35.495 --> 00:00:38.457
Right after supper Nancy crept up the back stairs to the attic.

7
00:00:38.477 --> 00:00:43.881
"The poor lamb probably cried herself to sleep," Nancy said.

8
00:00:45.362 --> 00:00:47.203
She softly opened Pollyanna's door.

9
00:00:47.984 --> 00:00:50.005
The next moment she gave a frightened cry.

10
00:00:50.025 --> 00:00:52.927
"Pollyanna? Where are you?"

11
00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:59.272
Nancy looked in the closet, under the bed, and even in the trunk.

12
00:01:00.972 --> 00:01:03.094
Then she flew downstairs and out to the garden.

13
00:01:03.114 --> 00:01:07.577
"Tom! Pollyanna is missing!"

14
00:01:07.597 --> 00:01:11.900
"What?" Tom stopped tying some roses to a trellis.

15
00:01:16.403 --> 00:01:21.186
He scanned the horizon and pointed to a small figure silhouetted against the evening sky.

16
00:01:21.206 --> 00:01:25.169
"There she is—on top of that hill!"

17
00:01:25.189 --> 00:01:26.430
"Oh no!

18
00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:28.211
Miss Polly will see her!"

19
00:01:28.551 --> 00:01:29.192
Nancy said.

20
00:01:30.272 --> 00:01:31.633
"I don't want her to get a scolding.

21
00:01:32.473 --> 00:01:34.594
She's already in trouble for missing supper."

22
00:01:37.996 --> 00:01:41.597
By the time Nancy reached Pollyanna, the older girl was out of breath.

23
00:01:41.617 --> 00:01:48.421
"Pollyanna, you gave me a scare," Nancy said, panting.

24
00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:50.682
"I didn't know where you were!"

25
00:01:56.724 --> 00:02:01.766
"You don't need to worry about me," Pollyanna said as they came down the hill hand in hand.

26
00:02:01.786 --> 00:02:06.248
"Father and the Ladies' Aiders used to worry when I wandered off.

27
00:02:07.489 --> 00:02:09.730
Then they realized I always came back."

28
00:02:11.551 --> 00:02:14.132
"How did you leave your room without anyone seeing you?"

29
00:02:14.492 --> 00:02:15.192
Nancy asked.

30
00:02:15.212 --> 00:02:18.934
"I climbed down the tree outside my window."

31
00:02:18.954 --> 00:02:22.215
"Oh my goodness!"

32
00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:23.476
Nancy exclaimed.

33
00:02:24.908 --> 00:02:27.150
"I'd like to know what your aunt would say about that."

34
00:02:28.491 --> 00:02:30.092
Pollyanna patted Nancy's arm.

35
00:02:31.373 --> 00:02:33.635
"Then I'll tell Aunt Polly, so you can find out!"

36
00:02:35.276 --> 00:02:36.978
Nancy's eyes widened in alarm.

37
00:02:36.998 --> 00:02:38.579
"No, no!

38
00:02:38.919 --> 00:02:39.720
Don't do that!"

39
00:02:41.802 --> 00:02:43.583
Pollyanna looked surprised but she nodded.

40
00:02:43.603 --> 00:02:48.287
"You must be hungry," Nancy said quickly.

41
00:02:48.307 --> 00:02:53.151
"But Miss Polly said you must eat bread and milk in the kitchen because you were late for

42
00:02:53.231 --> 00:03:00.366
supper." "I like bread and milk," Pollyanna said happily as they entered the kitchen.

43
00:03:00.386 --> 00:03:04.448
"And I won't have any trouble being glad about eating with you."

44
00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:09.831
Nancy remembered Pollyanna's brave attempt to like her attic room.

45
00:03:12.032 --> 00:03:14.854
"You don't have any trouble being glad about most things."

46
00:03:16.675 --> 00:03:18.036
Pollyanna laughed softly.

47
00:03:18.056 --> 00:03:20.937
"That's the whole point of the game."

48
00:03:20.957 --> 00:03:23.198
"The game?"

49
00:03:23.879 --> 00:03:27.801
Nancy gave Pollyanna a puzzled look as she set bread and milk on the table.

50
00:03:27.821 --> 00:03:30.822
"Yes, the Glad Game!

51
00:03:31.362 --> 00:03:33.462
Father and I played it all the time."

52
00:03:36.063 --> 00:03:37.724
Pollyanna took a big drink of milk.

53
00:03:37.744 --> 00:03:41.345
"It all started when I wanted a doll.

54
00:03:42.625 --> 00:03:45.486
Every week Father looked in the donation box at church.

55
00:03:46.406 --> 00:03:51.628
There were all kinds of toys and clothes and other things in there, but no doll.

56
00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:56.622
Finally he brought home a pair of crutches that were just my size."

57
00:03:56.642 --> 00:03:59.724
"Crutches?" Nancy said.

58
00:03:59.744 --> 00:04:04.947
"Yes!" Pollyanna clapped her hands with glee.

59
00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:10.450
"It wasn't a doll, but Father said, 'Just be glad you don't need crutches!'

60
00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:15.392
And so we began playing a game to find things to be glad about.

61
00:04:16.533 --> 00:04:18.614
Sometimes it's difficult to think of something.

62
00:04:19.515 --> 00:04:21.656
But that makes the game even more fun!"

63
00:04:22.964 --> 00:04:24.284
Nancy was still skeptical.

64
00:04:24.304 --> 00:04:30.986
"It's going to be harder to play the game without Father," Pollyanna admitted.

65
00:04:31.006 --> 00:04:34.207
"But maybe Aunt Polly will play it with me."

66
00:04:34.227 --> 00:04:36.448
"I don't think so!"

67
00:04:36.788 --> 00:04:37.688
Nancy blurted out.

68
00:04:38.628 --> 00:04:42.510
Noticing the disappointment on Pollyanna's face, she quickly made a promise.

69
00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:45.450
"But I'll do my best to play it with you."

70
00:04:47.991 --> 00:04:50.752
That satisfied Pollyanna, who finished up her bread and milk.

71
00:04:52.908 --> 00:04:55.690
Then she went into the sitting room, where Aunt Polly was reading.

72
00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:59.714
"It's time for bed," Aunt Polly said.

73
00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:03.897
"I regret having to punish you on your first day here."

74
00:05:03.917 --> 00:05:07.580
"I was glad you did, Aunt Polly.

75
00:05:08.621 --> 00:05:10.863
I like bread and milk, and Nancy too.

76
00:05:11.823 --> 00:05:13.325
So don't feel bad about that."

77
00:05:15.847 --> 00:05:18.128
Pollyanna gave her aunt an affectionate hug.

78
00:05:18.148 --> 00:05:22.312
"I've had a wonderful time so far.

79
00:05:23.868 --> 00:05:26.250
I know I'm going to love living with you.

80
00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:27.091
Good night!"

81
00:05:27.111 --> 00:05:30.793
"What an unusual child!"

82
00:05:31.374 --> 00:05:34.336
Aunt Polly said to herself as Pollyanna ran from the room.

83
00:05:36.197 --> 00:05:39.620
But a few minutes later, Pollyanna was sobbing herself to sleep.

84
00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:41.821
"Oh, Father!"

85
00:05:42.302 --> 00:05:43.222
she said softly.

86
00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:50.308
"Even you would have trouble being glad about sleeping way up here by yourself."
